Hydra Engine is a fork of Ghidra (https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra), the
software reverse engineering framework developed by the National Security Agency. It is based on
Ghidra's `master` branch (12.3 DEV); the upstream commit each release is based on is named in
CHANGELOG.md, and upstream changes are merged in as they land. Ghidra's project format, decompiler,
analyzers, processor modules, loaders and scripting API are Ghidra's own, unchanged except as
listed below, and Hydra Engine depends on them. It is distributed under the same license as
Ghidra, the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE). Ghidra's own notice is in NOTICE, and the
licenses of the third-party components Ghidra uses are in the licenses/ and GPL/ directories; all
of them apply to Hydra Engine unchanged.

